tern\n        # Use get_by_role with 'generic' and filter by text\n        generic_elements = page.get_by_role(\"generic\")\n        for i in range(await generic_elements.count()):\n            element = generic_elements.nth(i)\n            text = await element.text_content()\n            if text and \"git@\" in text:\n                return text.strip()\n    \n    # If above fails, try to find any element with text containing the SSH clone command\n    all_elements = page.get_by_role(\"generic\")\n    for i in range(await all_elements.count()):\n        element = all_elements.nth(i)\n        text = await element.text_content()\n        if text and \"git@\" in text and \"clone\" in text.lower():\n            return text.strip()\n    \n    # If still not found, return a message\n    return \"SSH clone command not found on the page.\"\n</code>\n\n<exception>\n'TimeoutError': Locator.click: Timeout 5000ms exceeded.\nCall log:\n  - waiting for get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Super_Awesome_Robot\", exact=True)\n\n</exception>\n\n---\n\n<reasoning>\nI need to show the SSH clone command for 'Super_Awesome_Robot'. From the previous attempt, the navigate_to_project_details function timed out because it couldn't find a link with the exact name 'Super_Awesome_Robot'. Looking at the current accessibility tree, I can see multiple project links under headings, but 'Super_Awesome_Robot' is not listed. The tree shows projects like 'Byte Blaze / a11y-syntax-highlighting', 'Byte Blaze / a11y-webring.club', etc., but no 'Super_Awesome_Robot'. This suggests that the project might not be visible on the current page, possibly due to filtering or pagination. I should first check if 'Super_Awesome_Robot' exists by searching for it. The tree includes a 'searchbox' with role 'searchbox' and name 'Filter by name'. I can use this to filter projects. I'll type 'Super_Awesome_Robot' into the search box and wait for results. If the project appears, I can click its link to navigate to the project det